 allow for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the specification of metric modulations and other metric relationships, such as swing tempo marks where two","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"eighths are equated to a quarter note \/ eighth note triplet. Tied notes can be represented in both types of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"metronome marks by using the beat-unit-tied and metronome-tied elements. The parentheses attribute indicates","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whether or not to put the metronome mark in parentheses; its value is no if not specified. The print-object","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attribute is set to no in cases where the metronome element represents a relationship or range that is not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"displayed in the music notation.","type":"text"}],"title":"MXLMetronome","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLMetronome"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLMetronome"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome"}}}